def _update_next(self, current_time):
    if self._next_timeout <= current_time:
        callback_time_sec = self.callback_time / 1000.0
        time_elapsed = current_time - self._next_timeout
        if time_elapsed > 0:
            self._next_timeout = current_time + callback_time_sec
        else:
            self._next_timeout += callback_time_sec
```
This change should prevent the _next_timeout from not being updated when the time elapsed is less than the callback time. This was the cause of the error where the callbacks were being executed too often on Windows.

